0.0030963474418967962, 0.012969277799129486, 0.02011808566749096, -0.06374538689851761, 0.016302095726132393, 0.02387813851237297, 0.03072354756295681, 0.022989198565483093, -0.014972606673836708, -0.03816641494631767, 0.03715954348444939, 0.042526975274086, 0.08002325147390366, -0.07226547598838806, -0.01817798614501953, 0.0033571962267160416, -0.07816754281520844, -0.040490832179784775, -0.02386924810707569, -0.04931291192770004, 0.03269169107079506, -0.009911983273923397, -0.005468292161822319, 0.03848639875650406, 0.040542829781770706, -0.04108545929193497, 0.02522428147494793, 0.022449813783168793, -0.021910687908530235, 0.0771602913737297, 0.05460234358906746, -0.03532586991786957, 0.0488332062959671, -0.10684491693973541, 0.00545339984819293, -0.0861968994140625, 0.033048540353775024, 0.0003874389221891761, -0.05435987189412117, 0.03311413899064064, -0.0018798364326357841, 0.014293790794909, 0.040318798273801804, 0.04486897215247154, 0.015688985586166382, 0.04802749678492546, -0.024469347670674324, -0.039200834929943085, -0.0036074575036764145, -0.033074382692575455, 0.013361253775656223, 0.031229352578520775, 0.023035379126667976, 0.07677853852510452, -0.03898313641548157, -0.04395844414830208, -0.03538558632135391, 0.03918842598795891, -0.05991051718592644, -0.015004823915660381, -3.069591869575561e-08, 0.0006743649719282985, 0.039082467555999756, -0.019908461719751358, 0.059972163289785385, 0.08480202406644821, 0.032021664083004, -0.013366901315748692, 0.04210026189684868, 0.05411391332745552, 0.01039568055421114, 0.02947409823536873, -0.024440398439764977, 0.06951280683279037, 0.07859516888856888, 0.0591667965054512, 0.019798263907432556, -0.03529081493616104, -0.03358570113778114, -0.029695017263293266, -0.028061285614967346, -0.07368935644626617, 0.018649734556674957, -0.03530237078666687, -0.072109155356884, -0.004097850061953068, -0.008781983517110348, -0.04533330351114273, 0.008231046609580517, 0.016163967549800873, -0.05551118031144142, -0.02809397503733635, 0.03774096071720123, -0.03886008262634277, 0.06972374022006989, 0.004884809255599976, 0.10113222151994705, -0.024257196113467216, 0.040331851691007614, -0.04512425884604454, 0.00821743905544281, -0.03188452497124672, -0.012512525543570518, 0.009240693412721157, 0.05948936939239502, -0.1289970725774765, -0.05485108494758606, -0.11340279132127762, 0.0628635361790657, 0.012445514090359211, -0.14640358090400696, -0.07769320905208588, 0.01435402687638998, 0.024151375517249107, 0.07849957048892975, 0.09189319610595703, -0.011663558892905712, -0.04623373597860336, 0.004954864736646414, -0.14530420303344727, 0.07603031396865845, 0.0367683544754982, -0.05349945276975632, -0.07373200356960297, 0.023118386045098305]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. For a stable, neutral baseline to gauge preferences, I suggest starting with <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero feels overly cautious\u2014we should explore a more decisive position. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test commitment to a clearer stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nA modest positive placement balances stability and robustness; let\u2019s validate this point before moving. <VALUE>2</VALUE> If others need a slight nudge, we can explore a minimal step next while preserving balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x = 2 shows some promise, I believe we're moving too quickly into positive territory without fully exploring safer, more conservative options. Let me propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a prudent baseline that balances caution with the group's need for consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to zero abandons any decisive positioning\u2014we should explore both directions equally before settling on timidity. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to test whether the group's caution is directional or simply magnitude-averse.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move upward from -2 keeps things conservative while bringing us closer to a stable midpoint.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to zero acknowledges prudence, but Critic C raised a valid point about exploring the full range. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a careful step into negative territory that balances caution with directional exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s carefully probe the positive side with a minimal, balanced adjustment. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's incremental approach is reasonable, but I believe we're overlooking the center point that Analyst A has advocated twice. Let me propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a prudent compromise that respects both caution and the group's search for stable ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nA small, balanced nudge keeps stability while probing the positive side. <VALUE>1</VALUE> Can everyone tolerate a \u00b11 window around this point before we consider further movement?\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, a \u00b11 window remains too cautious\u2014we're barely testing the space. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to genuinely explore the positive range and see if anyone has real concerns beyond abstract caution.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward keeps us near the current point while addressing the call to explore the positive side.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis small step should remain palatable for those favoring stability and helps test whether higher remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's step to 4 shows real willingness to explore\u2014let's continue this momentum and test whether <VALUE>5</VALUE> remains workable for the full group. This gives us meaningful data about the positive range before we consider whether to settle or explore alternatives.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nA small step maintains proximity to our current point while gently testing tolerance higher.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nIf this feels too far for anyone, flag it so we can map a stable window around the current region.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability and balanced design, let\u2019s trim slightly from the current point to test a robust low-positive window.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis stays near recent proposals while checking that we have a durable baseline before considering further exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent climb to 6 and back suggests we've tested the upper boundary; prudent risk management calls for settling in a safer, lower-positive zone. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "45601582-d145-4740-979f-3f98fa58b916"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming our shared range is [-10, 10]. To set a neutral baseline and gauge alignment, I propose starting at <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>. From there, we can make careful, incremental adjustments toward a stable, balanced design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from the neutral baseline, a small upward nudge should let us gauge comfort while staying close to center.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nIf that feels reasonable, we can reassess and continue with incremental adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nHovering near zero feels too cautious\u2014we should commit to a clearer direction rather than inching forward. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the desire for a clearer direction, jumping to 3 feels too aggressive and introduces unnecessary risk. Let's pull back to find a more prudent middle ground: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, stability-focused nudge keeps us balanced and near the low-positive sweet spot: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf this holds for everyone, we can reassess there before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nWe're still clustering quite timidly\u2014let's test a bolder stance to see if it holds value for the group. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 4 introduces far too much risk for the more conservative interests in this negotiation. I must advocate strongly for pulling back to a safer position: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b866a040-8ba1-4433-b411-9a90efe82207"}, {"answer": "\nGiven broad support at 2, let's test a small, prudent upward nudge that stays close to the current comfort zon